# Individual: <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001674> (Gregorian Calendar)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001674> "The Gregorian Calendar was instituted by Pope Gregory XIII via papal bull on 24 February 1582 as a reform of the Julian Calendar to stop the drift of the calendar with respect to the equinoxes and solstices. The Gregorian Calendar is currently the most widely used civil Calendar System in the world and is 13 days ahead of the Julian Calendar Date."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001674> "Gregorian Calendar"@en)
